\pard\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\lang9 1)what is the super class of arraylist,Hashmap?\par
 Arraylist --> AbstractList --> AbstractCollection\par
HashMap --> AbstractMap \par
2)What is the finalize()?\par
Finalize() its present in the Object class. finalize() method is used to perform cleanup activities before an object is garbage collected, but it is deprecated and not recommended to use.\par
3)What is Iterator and ListIterator?\par
Iterator is used for forward traversal, while ListIterator allows both forward and backward traversal and works only with List.\par
4)what is Stringpool ?\par
The String Pool is a special memory area in the Java heap where String literals are stored. Its main purpose is to save memory by reusing immutable String objects.\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1 String s3 = new String("Java");\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}This creates a new object outside the String Pool\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Even though "Java" exists in the pool, new forces a new object\par

