\pard\sl240\slmult1 5)What are all the Wrapper classes? why its need ?\par
wrapper classes are predefined classes that convert primitive data types into objects.\par
Java provides one wrapper class for each primitive type in the java.lang package.\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Java is not 100% object\f1\_\f0 oriented because primitives are not objects.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Wrapper classes help bridge this gap.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}Because Java collections and frameworks work with objects, not primitive types.\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
6)What is this and super key words in java?\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 this refers to the current class object (the object that is calling the method or constructor).\par

\pard{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf2\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1 this() must be the first statement in the constructor.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}super refers to the immediate parent class object.\par
{\pntext\f2\'B7\tab}super() must be the first statement in the constructor.\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1 7)What is Object-oriented Programming language?\par
An object\f1\_\f0 oriented programming language is a language that uses objects and classes to represent real\f1\_\f0 world entities along with their data and behavior.\par

